    "question": {
      ":question/id": "305c5606-9900-5ae5-bc93-30cdbfd4d769",
      ":question/problem": "Which of the following matrices are in row echelon form?\n\nSelect all that apply.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Remember that a matrix is in row echelon form if it satisfies the following conditions:\n\nI. All the zero rows (rows with only zeros), if any, are placed at the *bottom* of the matrix.\n\nII. Each leading entry of a row is in a column *to the right* of the leading entry of the row above it.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each matrix in turn.\n\n- The matrix $A$ is not in row echelon form since the leading entry $a_{34}=-8$ is in the same column as the leading entry $a_{24}=-4$ (condition II is violated).\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}9 & 7 & 6 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- The matrix $B$ is not in row echelon form since the leading entry $b_{21}=5$ is in the same column as the leading entry $b_{11}=-8$ (condition II is violated).\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}-8 & 4 & 2 & -7 \\\\ 5 & 3 & 6 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- The matrix $C$ is not in row echelon form since the leading entry $c_{32}=4$ is in the same column as the leading entry $c_{22}=-6$ (condition II is violated).\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}-8 & -7 & -9 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -6 & -6 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 6 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -9\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTherefore, none of the matrices are in row echelon form.",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
